Quantum mechanics (@quantum-mechanics: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_3QKXAVG6MAM4QY6K34TH62J0H2
Quantum mechanics describes states, observables, probabilities, and dynamics at scales where classical models are insufficient. This material covers wave mechanics, spin, angular momentum, approximation, scattering, identical particles, and measurement, connecting mathematical structure with experiments and the interpretation of quantum predictions.

**Common preparation developed:** the [quantum foundations review](../core/Review-quantum-descriptions-with-their-physical-premises-and-evidence-limits.lingua) connects physical premises to the shared finite complex mathematics, including ideal measurement, mixtures, state-dependent uncertainty, Hamiltonian dynamics and a bounded continuous-well bridge. This prepares branch entry; full wave mechanics, angular momentum, approximation, scattering, identical particles and advanced formation remain pending.

**Parent:** [Physics — fields, matter, motion and physical evidence](../Physics.lingua#r_04A5CP8RTBERZEN4XCCDQ3T47W).
} r_3QKXAVG6MAM4QY6K34TH62J0H2
